{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic","id":1520861,"title":"Fallen magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-18T02:08:31-07:00","id":1520861,"title":"Fallen magic","content":"Is there a compilation somewhere of mortal magic?<br /> <br /> I think there is Sorcery (Mummy), Necromancy (Geist) and Shamanism(?) ( Werewolf), with open rites/ceremonies/rituals.<br /> <br /> But I want a comprehensive source for all these systems in one place and any more than i am missing? (like i think Mage allows sleepwalkers take astral adept, and Stigmatics get unseen sense of the g-d-Machine, but i don't think these minor powers really compare, nor are they applicable to all mortals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  fixing typos 08-18-2023, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T07:18:12-07:00","id":1520878,"title":"","content":"There is not a comprehensive source AFAIK. I would love one, but it just doesn't exist that I have found. And I know I certainly don't understand things nearly well enough to make such a list. <br /> <br /> Your list is also missing the basics that all mortals can do like summoning, binding, and warding from the default Chronicles book. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it really counts as mortal magic per se, but there is Shadow Occultism in Shunned by the Moon, which grants an essence pool, influence, expanded ability to learn and lead rites, and additional options to gain additional influences. It's human only for what that's worth, but it requires you to have been ridden or claimed at some point so YMMV. <br /> <br /> There's the things from Hunter the Vigil that the various conspiracies can do, several of them are magical in nature. They require membership in an organization so again, I'm not sure if that's what you're looking for or not. <br /> <br /> If you're willing to include 3PP then there's Thaumaturgy in the Second Sight Third Eye book, which is basically the first edition Second Sight book updated to 2nd edition. It was done by Chris Falco.There's all kinds of other stuff as well, blood magic and what not, in 3rd party publications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T19:06:57-07:00","id":1520917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic#post1520861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is Sorcery (Mummy), Necromancy (Geist) and Shamanism(?) ( Werewolf), with open rites/ceremonies/rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcery and Ceremonies are functionally different mechanical takes on the same phenomenon; what the God-Machine does with occult matrices are a third take that doesn't have consistent hard mechanics due to it being a plot device.<br /> <br /> Pack Rites are largely distinguished from the above by their ability to mess with the Shadow and corresponding requirement of a connection thereto.<br /> <br /> Blood sorcery is likewise little different from the regular magic anyone can make use of apart from the application of channels and resources and training largely practiced by vampires and their ilk \u2014 the Sons of Phobos use similar methods with grislier costs than most.<br /> <br /> Awakened magic is mostly different from worldly magic in the lack of a strict need for most of the components that the above leverage to produce an effect \u2014 to be very loose about it, in replicating a Closed Rite the Awakened soul is functionally substituting Pillars for gestures/ingredients/timing constraints and hoping the world doesn't catch them out.<br /> <br /> The Obcasus Rites of the Begotten are technically the opposite of &quot;mortal magic,&quot; being the exclusive domain of monsters who no longer have a whole individual human soul, possessed of knowledge from communion with fear itself and conducting the ritual in a claimed place of supernatural power and importance; mortal assistance is arguably the least efficient means of mitigating penalties to the rolls to conduct the rites, to say nothing of uninvited guests getting into and out of the temple.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's worth asking what your actual goal is in seeking a compilation of &quot;mortal magic,&quot; because as a category that's not really useful unless you're doing an extremely loose crossover game where the fact that theoretically any effect can be produced from a number of different ludonarrative frameworks is winning out over the general preferability that such systems as are used in a game for a single purpose be elegantly made. Sorcery is made to serve the purposes of sorcerers in a Mummy game, while Ceremonies are made to serve the needs of krewes in a Geist game, just as skinchangers and Shadow Occultists use different systems, and as ever, a Merit-based microtemplate is typically the means of enabling access to a variety of powers with the least amount of homebrew effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T20:30:10-07:00","id":1520920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520917#post1520917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> It's worth asking what your actual goal is in seeking a compilation of &quot;mortal magic,&quot; because as a category that's not really useful</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you say stuff like this? It comes off as extremely condescending and rude when you tell people what they're doing for their game isn't useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T22:12:44-07:00","id":1520922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520920#post1520920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you say stuff like this? It comes off as extremely condescending and rude when you tell people what they're doing for their game isn't useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrariwise, it comes off as extremely confrontational when you chop my statement in half for the sake of calling me rude; the rest of the sentence offers contextualizing detail to that particular statement that I should hope makes it clear I am attempting to help identify what the focal purpose is to avoid misapplying effort.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness is a setting where &quot;mortal magic&quot; can hypothetically do anything with sufficient complexity and symbolic weight behind it because that's how magic in general works and the systems behind them are built for different gamelines more to serve those lines' themes and mechanical frameworks than to model substantially different phenomena. That is the entire point of the short list preceding my saying &quot;stuff like&quot; &quot;the category of magic that is not specific to a type of monster and can be used by mortals is [so broad as to be] not very useful for practical applications unless you specifically aren't bothered by those different systems modeling similar effects from the same source in mechanically different ways.&quot;<br /> <br /> The systems for Sorcery are in Mummy. The systems for Ceremonies are in Geist. Both describe Abjuration et al as their type of magic in a sufficiently widespread form that a character needs no special investment to perform them with a certain degree of circumstantial unpredictability not accorded specific game mechanics. Ceremonies have dot ratings that affect their time investment but can be learned by anyone and are taught for free to krewe members of sufficient Mystery Cult Initiation, while Closed Rites use the Rule of Three and require one to be a sorcerer to learn and have no direct relation to Scorpion Cult Initiation. Both do not rely on any sort of internal quality of the ritualist(s) and are instead making use of esoteric ways the world works which theoretically anyone could follow with the proper knowledge.<br /> <br /> There is narratively no reason not to pick one or the other or substitute a Merit-based model in a crossover game where you are not specifically playing a celebrant from a krewe or a sorcerer; a compilation of the different systems does not exist largely because if you're playing a game where such a system exists or using a supplement that introduces such a system, you do not typically need a different system outside of very haphazard crossover play.<br /> <br /> I say the category is not really useful outside of circumstances that do not seem germane to the main purpose of compiling a list of a given category of game items because without knowing what the goal is I am not privy to the use such a compilation could provide, which is why I said it was worth asking what the actual goal was. Hope that clears that up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T23:47:45-07:00","id":1520924,"title":"","content":"Fore the aim is to understand. I think the end result would be interesting mortal characters who can do some magic.<br /> <br /> That could be mortals in a Mage game where they might exist as minor members of an order, perhaps ignored by the awakened practicioners until they cause a mystery. Or maybe in a mystery Cult or working for the Seers.<br /> <br /> It could be used in the context of a mortal game without anyone playing awakened characters, which could be used a number of ways, like a cosmic horror story or mortals seeking immortality... It could be mortals trying to protect themselves from monsters, or just seeking power for its own sake.<br /> <br /> But the immediate goal is to understand what systems are already in place, and to tie them together (with some homebrew if necessary) so they can be used as a cohesive whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T00:02:58-07:00","id":1520925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520922#post1520922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrariwise, it comes off as extremely confrontational when you chop my statement in half for the sake of calling me rude; the rest of the sentence offers contextualizing detail to that particular statement that I should hope makes it clear I am attempting to help identify what the focal purpose is to avoid misapplying effort.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness is a setting where &quot;mortal magic&quot; can hypothetically do anything with sufficient complexity and symbolic weight behind it because that's how magic in general works and the systems behind them are built for different gamelines more to serve those lines' themes and mechanical frameworks than to model substantially different phenomena. That is the entire point of the short list preceding my saying &quot;stuff like&quot; &quot;the category of magic that is not specific to a type of monster and can be used by mortals is [so broad as to be] not very useful for practical applications unless you specifically aren't bothered by those different systems modeling similar effects from the same source in mechanically different ways.&quot;<br /> <br /> The systems for Sorcery are in Mummy. The systems for Ceremonies are in Geist. Both describe Abjuration et al as their type of magic in a sufficiently widespread form that a character needs no special investment to perform them with a certain degree of circumstantial unpredictability not accorded specific game mechanics. Ceremonies have dot ratings that affect their time investment but can be learned by anyone and are taught for free to krewe members of sufficient Mystery Cult Initiation, while Closed Rites use the Rule of Three and require one to be a sorcerer to learn and have no direct relation to Scorpion Cult Initiation. Both do not rely on any sort of internal quality of the ritualist(s) and are instead making use of esoteric ways the world works which theoretically anyone could follow with the proper knowledge.<br /> <br /> There is narratively no reason not to pick one or the other or substitute a Merit-based model in a crossover game where you are not specifically playing a celebrant from a krewe or a sorcerer; a compilation of the different systems does not exist largely because if you're playing a game where such a system exists or using a supplement that introduces such a system, you do not typically need a different system outside of very haphazard crossover play.<br /> <br /> I say the category is not really useful outside of circumstances that do not seem germane to the main purpose of compiling a list of a given category of game items because without knowing what the goal is I am not privy to the use such a compilation could provide, which is why I said it was worth asking what the actual goal was. Hope that clears that up!</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if you are being condescending or not. I like Mage, and its magic system only lacks any interesting fallen magic (hence the thread title) and the main reason for that is the limited value mortal sorcerers would play in a Mage game (while the supremacy of Supernal magic was on display).<br /> <br /> Wanting a comprehensible system is an aim in itself for me. I would really like to include Occult Matrices, but them not having any system (beyond suborning them for Demons to mis-use) is really annoying. I understand the Ludo-narrative reasons - mostly the G-d Machine not being meant to be comprehensible. But I would love to see Demons teaching humans to create Occult Matrices and/or mortals otherwise doing interesting things in a given game (perhaps creating an Angel - whether it could become Unchained or not as plot).<br /> <br /> At the most abstract, from a storyteller perspective, i want a solid base of what can be done and how by character in order to come up with plot. Understanding the physics/magic/mechanics of a given setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T05:28:31-07:00","id":1520936,"title":"","content":"There is also the Merit based Blood Chymistry, from Spilled blood, very interesting for a Vampire/Promethean crossover","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T09:21:10-07:00","id":1520951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520925#post1520925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't tell if you are being condescending or not. I like Mage, and its magic system only lacks any interesting fallen magic (hence the thread title) and the main reason for that is the limited value mortal sorcerers would play in a Mage game (while the supremacy of Supernal magic was on display).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage does not provide in-book examples of unAwakened magic use because it has a comprehensive system for building effects with Awakened magic and sticking symbolic scaffolding and weird hiccups onto it; you can use that existing system as the basis for building an effect, adding or subtracting complications, and stating that the result is not Awakened magic for the purposes of game mechanics. This is the same reason multiple books have suggested making Numina by copying other supernatural abilities or personalizing Dread Powers by setting dicepools and applying use restrictions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wanting a comprehensible system is an aim in itself for me. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the comprehensible system is &quot;just about anything can be made to happen with enough connective tissue and legwork.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would really like to include Occult Matrices, but them not having any system (beyond suborning them for Demons to mis-use) is really annoying. I understand the Ludo-narrative reasons - mostly the G-d Machine not being meant to be comprehensible. But I would love to see Demons teaching humans to create Occult Matrices and/or mortals otherwise doing interesting things in a given game (perhaps creating an Angel - whether it could become Unchained or not as plot). </div> </div> </div>The problem here, in addition to the aforementioned &quot;this can be literally anything,&quot; is that by default the God-Machine is the deciding factor for whether an attempted occult matrix produces an output. Highly seasoned individual demons and the Deva Corporation might have figured out some very specific forms of currently-reliable occult matrices, but the current system is &quot;the God-Machine put together a literal or metaphorical device that does something, and by examining the symbolic interactions of its component parts a character can alter those components and their arrangement to alter their effects.&quot; Every occult matrix is a plot device whose mechanics are specific to that manifestation of the God-Machine's arcane physics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the most abstract, from a storyteller perspective, i want a solid base of what can be done and how by character in order to come up with plot. Understanding the physics/magic/mechanics of a given setting. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside &quot;it's literally anything you can justify&quot; for a moment, it would be helpful to address the apparent contradiction between &quot;Merits like Astral Adept aren't applicable to all mortals&quot; and &quot;sorcery counts,&quot; because that gets into the fuzzy state of template-specificity in the current state of the franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T10:14:11-07:00","id":1520954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520951#post1520951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Setting aside &quot;it's literally anything you can justify&quot; for a moment, it would be helpful to address the apparent contradiction between &quot;Merits like Astral Adept aren't applicable to all mortals&quot; and &quot;sorcery counts,&quot; because that gets into the fuzzy state of template-specificity in the current state of the franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could allow any mortal access to the astral adept merit, maybe with some pre-requisites based on other meditation merits. But RAW only sleepwalkers and mages can take it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the sorcery related merit are something which RAW any human can take.<br /> <br /> Similarly Necromancy in Geist is something any mortal could learn, and Shadow Occultist which someone mentioned above is... Well messy, but in principle any mortal can debase themselves enough to accept essence from a patron spirit.<br /> <br /> I think anyone can take on goblin debt aswell, leaving mortal at risk of becoming hedge denizens... But I forget what I was reading about that in Dark Eras. Mostly because my thematic idea of a mortal sorcerer/mystical Cult doesn't include becoming a goblin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520936#post1520936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the Merit based Blood Chymistry, from Spilled blood, very interesting for a Vampire/Promethean crossover</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this merit to be found? I haven't read any recent vampire stuff or any Promethean stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T13:37:00-07:00","id":1520975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520954#post1520954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could allow any mortal access to the astral adept merit, maybe with some pre-requisites based on other meditation merits. But RAW only sleepwalkers and mages can take it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the sorcery related merit are something which RAW any human can take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except any character with an internal supernatural power is a Sleepwalker and there's a Merit for counting as a Sleepwalker from repeated exposure to Supernal or Abyssal phenomena and that's a sight broader to run across than a character with three dots in Occult and a relevant specialty as far as commonality goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly Necromancy in Geist is something any mortal could learn, </div> </div> </div>I would like to point out again that the term is just Ceremonies. You can do necromancy with Ceremonies, and Geist includes a number of rituals to that end, but making a blank page show the surface thoughts of whoever's bloody thumbprint is pressed onto it or connecting a call to the nearest phone to a target isn't necromancy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and Shadow Occultist which someone mentioned above is... Well messy, but in principle any mortal can debase themselves enough to accept essence from a patron spirit. </div> </div> </div>To reiterate: if Shadow Occultism, which requires undergoing a breaking point, gives you a Bane, and applies Tilts and Conditions when the Essence pool it gives you is too full, counts as &quot;Fallen magic,&quot; but Astral Adept, which can be qualified for by getting any other internal supernatural power or undergoing three breaking points that just about any mage can provide, does not, then this definition needs further clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think anyone can take on goblin debt aswell, leaving mortal at risk of becoming hedge denizens... But I forget what I was reading about that in Dark Eras. Mostly because my thematic idea of a mortal sorcerer/mystical Cult doesn't include becoming a goblin. </div> </div> </div>For that you want fae-touched/the Avowed, who simply are able to be taught Contracts, including Goblin Contracts. Given that the primary usage of Goblin Debt for people who can't vent it into bad luck and Conditions is having an IOU for services rendered that they need to make good on before or after they become a Hedge Denizen, I'm not sure I would call that &quot;magic&quot; except in the sense that a magical actor is involved in the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is this merit to be found? I haven't read any recent vampire stuff or any Promethean stuff. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/303157/Night-Horrors-Spilled-Blood\" target=\"_blank\">Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</a>, as named.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T13:50:55-07:00","id":1520977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520975#post1520975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.I would like to point out again that the term is just Ceremonies. You can do necromancy with Ceremonies, and Geist includes a number of rituals to that end, but making a blank page show the surface thoughts of whoever's bloody thumbprint is pressed onto it or connecting a call to the nearest phone to a target isn't necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might be one of the biggest failings of Geist, because according to the game that is necromancy. In WoD necromancy felt like necromancy, in CofD it feels totally random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T18:30:53-07:00","id":1520998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520977#post1520977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this might be one of the biggest failings of Geist, because according to the game that is necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. The game uses &quot;necromancy&quot; in the Ceremonies section twice: once in the description for the Ghost Trap Ceremony and once in an offhand fashion talking about &quot;self-taught necromancers&quot; stumbling through their own symbolism in the same way that different krewes teach different versions of the same Ceremony; the latter is on the same page as the sidebar specifically talking about how Ceremonies aren't powered by the Bargain or the geist and are just part of the way the world works. Bits of the way the world works have to do with the Underworld, sure, and some of those are necromancy, but Ceremonies are no more necromancy than highway driving is motorcycle ownership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T19:32:50-07:00","id":1521002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520998#post1520998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it isn't. The game uses &quot;necromancy&quot; in the Ceremonies section twice: once in the description for the Ghost Trap Ceremony and once in an offhand fashion talking about &quot;self-taught necromancers&quot; stumbling through their own symbolism in the same way that different krewes teach different versions of the same Ceremony; the latter is on the same page as the sidebar specifically talking about how Ceremonies aren't powered by the Bargain or the geist and are just part of the way the world works. Bits of the way the world works have to do with the Underworld, sure, and some of those are necromancy, but Ceremonies are no more necromancy than highway driving is motorcycle ownership.</div> </div> </div> </div>After digging more into it I believe we are both correct. The term necromancer is used repeatedly in the text to describe human antagonists who practice ceremonies. It also uses the term ritualist once, and gives examples of people who may practice ceremonies that aren't necromancers, like priests. Some ceremonies are necromancy, but not all of them are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T00:28:22-07:00","id":1521012,"title":"","content":"The gathering and usage of Mementos could count as necromancy if we squint at it, considering all the deathly stuff they\u2019re associated with. <br /> <br /> In fact, I suspect a lot of \u2018mortal magic\u2019 outside those represented by Supernatural Merits (and arguably, hunter Endowments) are based on magical items; fetishes, talens, Imbued &amp; Enhanced Items, Artifacts, Athanors, Hedgespun items, Tokens, Mementos, Vessels (both Vestiges and Relics), Gadgets, and whatever outside those categories that Hunter calls Bygones.<br /> <br /> (I think not all of the above are usable by mortals, though? Gonna have to check later)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T01:46:54-07:00","id":1521014,"title":"","content":"Yeah, i have an idea for magic items, but I would want things which mortals can create (which Afaik includes vestiges, tokens, maybe mementos and possibly fetishes/talens) but that is a whole seperate question.<br /> <br /> I am pretty sure Necromancy is defined in Geist as humans using magic to gain power from the dead. So a priest carrying out a passing on ceremony is helping the dead but wouldn't count as doing Necromancy.<br /> <br /> Necromancers derive their power from taking ghosts and abusing them. This is very much a socially defined convention to give Sin-eaters an interesting antagonist. But from a meta-magical perspective it places them akin to Shadow Occultists, as mortals who have found a external source of power they can tap.<br /> <br /> Sleepwalkers are not the same, mostly because they aren't going out and looking for power, developing a magic system or Cult based around some magical item.<br /> <br /> They can do these things, but that is not what defines a sleepwalker. Necromancers and Shadow Occultists are clearly differentiated. But I am happy to include Priests doing rituals in the list of magic users. Or pretty much any other magic user i can find rules for.<br /> <br /> Going to the Astral is something that would be interesting, but I'm not sure the same kind of power can be derived from it as the Shadow or Underworld (apart maybe from the well spring, but i suspect that leads to awakened magic).<br /> <br /> I would be pretty happy with a dream/astral based mortal sub-template (is that what we call these?) But I want to start with a base of RAW to ground any homebrewing.<br /> <br /> Like Sleepwalkers Stigmatics would not really count, but you could have a Stigmatic in magic cult trying to use other occult powers to take control of a piece of infrastructure/gain power from the god-machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T04:17:03-07:00","id":1521022,"title":"","content":"The book discussed humans who collect mementos under the heading grave robbers, necromancers were a separate section. But you bring up a good point, the use of items of power, whatever their name and origin, may often be passed off as magic in the hands of mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T12:26:11-07:00","id":1521051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521014#post1521014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, i have an idea for magic items, but I would want things which mortals can create (which Afaik includes vestiges, tokens, maybe mementos and possibly fetishes/talens) but that is a whole seperate question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fetish Rite is a Wolf Rite and the only way a mortal can create a token is by leaving something in the Hedge and then retrieving it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am pretty sure Necromancy is defined in Geist as humans using magic to gain power from the dead. So a priest carrying out a passing on ceremony is helping the dead but wouldn't count as doing Necromancy. </div> </div> </div>The word &quot;necromancy&quot; shows up exactly once in Geist 2e Core, and it's as the thing the Never-Born archetype of Absent ghost is obsessed with from the other side. The Lexicon defines &quot;necromancer&quot; as &quot;a general term for any living magician who interacts with (and usually exploits) the dead regularly.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Necromancers derive their power from taking ghosts and abusing them. This is very much a socially defined convention to give Sin-eaters an interesting antagonist. But from a meta-magical perspective it places them akin to Shadow Occultists, as mortals who have found a external source of power they can tap. </div> </div> </div>You are crossing wires between necromancers and Eaters of the Dead, who Shadow Occultists sit closer to in mechanical and thematic terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sleepwalkers are not the same, mostly because they aren't going out and looking for power, developing a magic system or Cult based around some magical item.<br /> <br /> They can do these things, but that is not what defines a sleepwalker. Necromancers and Shadow Occultists are clearly differentiated. But I am happy to include Priests doing rituals in the list of magic users. Or pretty much any other magic user i can find rules for. </div> </div> </div>I cannot tell if the capital &quot;P&quot; in Priest is mere arbitrary capitalization or invention of a systems term wholesale, but in any case I am still not seeing where the line is drawn between &quot;generic magic 'anyone' can use&quot; and &quot;this is a template or requires becoming technically part of another world&quot; as far as what does and doesn't count as a &quot;magic user.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going to the Astral is something that would be interesting, but I'm not sure the same kind of power can be derived from it as the Shadow or Underworld (apart maybe from the well spring, but i suspect that leads to awakened magic). </div> </div> </div>The Wellspring is in the Anima Mundi. Anyone who can access the Temenos has the capacity to get information they wouldn't otherwise have and make changes to the social reality of a potentially quite large chunk of the population by messing with the narratives shared between a group about a subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like Sleepwalkers Stigmatics would not really count, but you could have a Stigmatic in magic cult trying to use other occult powers to take control of a piece of infrastructure/gain power from the god-machine. </div> </div> </div>So we are once again butting up against &quot;trying to manipulate the ST-controlled interlocking collection of plot-devices counts, as does mutilating yourself through a spiritual patron, but indebting your way into dependence on the Hedge doesn't and neither does being a marked part of the God-Machine with access to Supernatural Merits.&quot; This is a frustratingly inconsistent variety of I-know-it-when-I-see-it when you are asking after a compilation of <i>mechanics</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T14:30:04-07:00","id":1521068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521051#post1521051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fetish Rite is a Wolf Rite and the only way a mortal can create a token is by leaving something in the Hedge and then retrieving it.<br /> <br /> The word &quot;necromancy&quot; shows up exactly once in Geist 2e Core, and it's as the thing the Never-Born archetype of Absent ghost is obsessed with from the other side. The Lexicon defines &quot;necromancer&quot; as &quot;a general term for any living magician who interacts with (and usually exploits) the dead regularly.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are crossing wires between necromancers and Eaters of the Dead, who Shadow Occultists sit closer to in mechanical and thematic terms.<br /> <br /> I cannot tell if the capital &quot;P&quot; in Priest is mere arbitrary capitalization or invention of a systems term wholesale, but in any case I am still not seeing where the line is drawn between &quot;generic magic 'anyone' can use&quot; and &quot;this is a template or requires becoming technically part of another world&quot; as far as what does and doesn't count as a &quot;magic user.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Wellspring is in the Anima Mundi. Anyone who can access the Temenos has the capacity to get information they wouldn't otherwise have and make changes to the social reality of a potentially quite large chunk of the population by messing with the narratives shared between a group about a subject.<br /> <br /> So we are once again butting up against &quot;trying to manipulate the ST-controlled interlocking collection of plot-devices counts, as does mutilating yourself through a spiritual patron, but indebting your way into dependence on the Hedge doesn't and neither does being a marked part of the God-Machine with access to Supernatural Merits.&quot; This is a frustratingly inconsistent variety of I-know-it-when-I-see-it when you are asking after a compilation of <i>mechanics</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, was i not clear, becoming a Stigmatic on its own doesn't make one a magic user. But it also doesn't preclude one from becoming a magic user.<br /> <br /> I did read some of the stuff about Werewolf rites, and i am pretty sure the explaination about wolf-blooded having a 'change' is relevant (even though again, wolf-blooded come in the same category as Stigmatics) - ie you lose your mortal powers when you change. A wolf-blood may become a ghoul/vampire/Werewolf/awakened mage, but once they do they stop being what they are.<br /> <br /> Stop being able to do the other things (a mechanic based on some real history of setting). So a wolf-blooded who becomes a vampire can't then go through the first change and become a werewolf-vampire.<br /> <br /> Either way, they can still perform most rituals (Necromantic or Sorcerous) and as a vampire like have access to blood magic.<br /> <br /> But I'm not interested in blood magic because it is only available to vampires.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could put this in the same category as Shadow Occultists, where anyone can go out and find a spirit patron - likewise anyone can go out and get embraced... Whereas not everyone can go out and perform wolf/pack rites (though Shadow Occultists get to perform pack rites at least).<br /> <br /> So we have a few criteria,<br /> 1) initiation (usually some cost/merit bought)<br /> 2) powers learnt (usually seperate powers/rituals)<br /> 3) ritual cost (usually willpower/essence)<br /> <br /> I am not sure what the initiation for acquiring goblin debt would be, I'm not sure how I feel about including hobs as human magicians.<br /> <br /> Shadow Occultist fits neatly.<br /> <br /> Fitful sleeper is on, but there is no obvious way to gain the astral adept merit (it is something which just happens, not which you can learn from a teacher... So is up to the ST).<br /> <br /> Necromantic ceremonies* seem to have to lowest level of initiation, though joining a Krewe is certainly a fast track.<br /> <br /> Sorcery merit from Mummy are similar , but joining a Mummy's Cult replacing the Krewe.<br /> <br /> Am i missing anything?<br /> <br /> The Sons of Photos?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T16:21:47-07:00","id":1521081,"title":"","content":"In addition to the 2e shadow occultists, I liked the 1e Book of Spirits; it had a lot of stuff you could just do to perceive or interact with the Shadow that you didn't need to buy with Merit dots or have too many other rules for. Like if you stabbed yourself in the eye with a needle in just the right way you could see into the Shadow with that eye for a little while; things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T16:30:07-07:00","id":1521083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521081#post1521081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the 2e shadow occultists, I liked the 1e Book of Spirits; it had a lot of stuff you could just do to perceive or interact with the Shadow that you didn't need to buy with Merit dots or have too many other rules for. Like if you stabbed yourself in the eye with a needle in just the right way you could see into the Shadow with that eye for a little while; things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the kind of spirit stuff i like, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T17:24:32-07:00","id":1521086,"title":"","content":"I want to point out that many necromancers aren't part of a krewe, and many sorcerers aren't in a mummy's cult. You can find the ceremonies or whatever in a variety of forms and learn them without supernatural assistance. <br /> <br /> It's also worth pointing out that wolf blooded retain their tells when they gain a template other than werewolf. <br /> <br /> Have mortal alchemists been mentioned yet? I feel like they should count even though alchemy is a bit different from normal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T18:22:05-07:00","id":1521088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521086#post1521086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to point out that many necromancers aren't part of a krewe, and many sorcerers aren't in a mummy's cult. You can find the ceremonies or whatever in a variety of forms and learn them without supernatural assistance.<br /> <br /> It's also worth pointing out that wolf blooded retain their tells when they gain a template other than werewolf.<br /> <br /> Have mortal alchemists been mentioned yet? I feel like they should count even though alchemy is a bit different from normal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, yes, the mortal alchemists from Promethean.<br /> Personally I'm a fan of the fact that there is no unified &quot;magic system&quot; for the Chronicles of Darkness, that there's all these weird little fractured traditions all over the place that seem to be drawing on similar principles but come at it from different directions. Like just for alchemists there's the alchemical tradition of the Prometheans and the mortal alchemists who hunt them, there's the Mesen-Nebu mummies who practice pre-Egyptian alchemy and teach some of its principles to their followers, and the Awakened call it alchemy when they imbue their own magic into potions and unguents and so on. And the Ascending Ones from Hunter, with their characteristic mix of internal and external alchemy. And the Ascending Ones from Hunter, with their characteristic mix of internal and external alchemy. And these all have different systems, but if you look at them all you can see commonalities and maybe even come up with a tentative timeline of which tradition may have cross-pollinated with another one.<br /> The Blood Bathers in the 1e Immortals book as a pretty evocative description of how Blood Bathers discover their bathing rituals, and it stuck with me as an edifying example of how ritual behavior in this setting can lead to magical rituals with clear effects on the world. Like, if you're already superstitious or inclined to ritual behavior, sometimes your idiosyncratic ritual just flips a cosmic switch and starts to do something, and from then on you can repeat that effect as long as you perfectly replicate the conditions of that first successful ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 08-20-2023, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T19:13:26-07:00","id":1521092,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mortal magic&quot; in CoD is mostly undefined. I think Hurt Locker has the most on the actual subject, and that is more incidental than anything else. Unless we count Endowments in Hunter the Vigil.<br /> <br /> That said, there is a lot of other kinds of magic that can and do hook into and build upon said magic. (Mummy) Ritual Sorcery and Necromancer Ceromonies are the most obvious, but they are very different in metaphysical terms. They also tend to fall into 'draw power from elsewhere to empower what was already there&quot;. (Duat for Sorcery and the Underworld for Ceromonies).<br /> If pressed, I would consider Ceromonies to be closer to mortal magic, as the Underworld could be argued to be part of the Phenomenonal/Fallen World the same way the Shadow/Hisil is. While neither require membership (unlike Werewolf's Rites), they are still not connected directly to the 'mortal' world of CoD. This applies to Shadow Occultists (see NH:Shunned by the Moon) and Alchemists (Promethean 2e; subset called Insatiable) fall into similar categories while also being prone to mental instability, if not psychopathy.<br /> <br /> Fun Fact: even Open Rites from Werewolf require you to have a totem spirit; the Pack even has a merit that allows fully human 'packs' to to take a totem and use said Rites as it's main benefit.<br /> <br /> Most magic in the setting that mortals can use is usually filtered through another entity. Heck, the Changeling splat itself is almost exclusively using such filtered magic (Contracts). Overusing such magic is called out as a potential Divergence in Deviant. <br /> Come to think of it, magic in CoD is very transformative. Drink vamp blood? No longer purely mortal. Touch a strange gear sticking out of the Church basement? Now you see mechanisms of False Heaven. See a wolf-monster? Congrats, the wolf is now in your blood. Stay too long in the world hidden in your closet? Congrats on being the Queen of the Goblins there, (ok this one is properly your fault). <br /> <br /> Ritual Sorcey and Necromantic Ceremonies are among the few systems of magic that are accessible to mortals and don't inherently change them into something else...well aside from Sleepwalkers. But pretty much everything turns a baseline into a Sleepwalker. <i>Benedictions</i> turn a human into a Sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> Which brings me back to Hunter. Hunter is Blue Book+ in CoD. Normal humans encountering the supernatural and stepping up in how to deal with it. H:tV just assumes you've done that first Story at character creation, whereas the Chronicles book is essentially built for preludes. As you go up in tiers in Hunter, you tie yourself more closely to certain aspects of the setting that aren't present/noticeable from a Blue Book perspective, (as community is a big theme in Hunter). At tier 3 you can get an Endowment from your Conspiracy. 99% of Endownments are magic. All Endowments are intended for use by human mortals, and I would look at any requests for exceptions very closely.<br /> If need be, Endowments are my first choice for canonical system of magic for mundanes. <br /> That said, 1st edition's Second Sight was exactly the kind of thing that is perfect for this. An unoffical update to this book exists on the Vault called <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/260310/Second-Sight-Third-Eye?term=second+&amp;filters=0_0_45760_0_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Second Sight: Third Eye</a>.<br /> <br /> On the subject of alchemy, there are at least 4 kinds listed in CoD and all of them can (technically) be used by baseline mortal humans.<ul><li>Promethean style Alchemy involves Pyros to mimic the Transmutations of the gameline's protagonists. Mostly unclear on how it works, the sample antagonist does not follow the suggested rules and most depictions in the book are called out as crazy fanatics willing to do terrible things. Justified by selected bias; sane alchemists would not hunt Prometheans and generally be Antagonists to them. (At least, no more likely than anyone else and may in fact, be able to recognize Disquiet, maybe even have a plan to deal with it.) Not recommended for players.</li> <li>The Ascending Ones Conspiracy in Hunter the Vigil practice a kind of alchemy. Works fine for PCs.</li> <li>The Mesen-Nebu Guild of Irem's Arisen practiced a kind of Alchemy. While it has largely been unsupported mechanically, 1st edition implied it was in fact, a subset or style of Ritual Sorcery, much like creating a Vestiges is in 2e. This would produce Relics if done on the same scale. Heck, we have an outline for pyropus (M:tC pg 224) if we were to create a ritual for it. However this is largely not explored in the texts, so for now it is not recommended for players.</li> <li>'Supernal' Alchemy (Signs of Sorcery) does not <i>technically </i>require Awakened magic. All you need to do is take the (mostly) pure material over near-dimensional boundaries every few days over a relatively short period (around a month). I'd argue that Uratha and Sin-Eaters should have more access to this stuff than Mages, but since anyone can open a gate to the Underworld with its corresponding key, this is open mundanes as well. Perfectly fine for players.</li> </ul>Have fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T19:17:14-07:00","id":1521094,"title":"","content":"Nearly every gameline has its own brand of \u201cmortal magic\u201d, several in the form of mortals who have access to the magic of the gameline's protagonists: Vampire has the Sons of Phobos (mortals with access to Cr\u00faac); Werewolf has Wolf-blooded ritemasters; Mage has Proximi: Promethean has alchemists: Changeling has the Fae-Touched; Geist has ceremonies; Mummy has Sorcery; and so on. <br /> <br /> But the big one that kills any possibility of a comprehensive list of mortal magic is Hunter. <i>At least </i>two of the Endowments from that book are, in effect, mortal magic; and the book is designed to let the Storyteller come up with his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T20:02:13-07:00","id":1521096,"title":"","content":"I noticed certain themes keep cropping up. <br /> <br /> 1) Mortal magic that requires you to be born into them. Lucifuge or Wolf Blooded Rites. <br /> <br /> 2) Mortal Magic that allows you to gain power from somewhere else or something else. Shadow occultists / necromancers. <br /> <br /> 3) Magic you can gain through learning. Blue book rituals like summoning or warding. <br /> <br /> 4) Magic of things. The use of magical items or magic within items. Alchemy, mementos, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T00:54:27-07:00","id":1521106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521094#post1521094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the big one that kills any possibility of a comprehensive list of mortal magic is Hunter. <i>At least </i>two of the Endowments from that book are, in effect, mortal magic; and the book is designed to let the Storyteller come up with his own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider that the opposite of a problem, as there must be some ST guidance on how to come up with your own, and if anything that is the ultimate goal of a comprehensive system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nearly every gameline has its own brand of \u201cmortal magic\u201d, several in the form of mortals who have access to the magic of the gameline's protagonists: Vampire has the Sons of Phobos (mortals with access to Cr\u00faac); Werewolf has Wolf-blooded ritemasters; Mage has Proximi: Promethean has alchemists: Changeling has the Fae-Touched; Geist has ceremonies; Mummy has Sorcery; and so on. </div> </div> </div>Not all of these are alike. Yes, each game l\u00edne has created some sub-category like their template. But Wolf-blooded and Proximi are not 'just humans', they are excluded by the 'anyone can do it' requirement.<br /> <br /> Sons of Phobos and Shadow Occultist both change the practicioners, but anyone can just learn the practices. So they fit with Geist's ceremonies (which are not all Necromancy, but i am calling Necromancy to help distinguish them) and Mummy's Sorcery.<br /> <br /> I think Fae-touched are an edge case... But I'm not sure about including Goblin Debt.<br /> <br /> So we have:<br /> Blood Sorcery* (and the heart stealing ritual which is called out as not being blood sorcery),<br /> Sorcery,<br /> Necromancy,<br /> Alchemy,<br /> Shadow rites/patronage (i have some questions about mortals forming an all human pack/cult and doing pack rites, is that only possible through the Shadow Occultist initiation?)<br /> Thaumatergy*,<br /> Endowments.<br /> <br /> *I think these are 1e/may need updating.<br /> <br /> We have two main types:<br /> Intrinsic changes to the world controlled by the magic user.<br /> Calling on the powers of other beings to change the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) Mortal magic that requires you to be born into them. Lucifuge or Wolf Blooded Rites.<br /> <br /> 2) Mortal Magic that allows you to gain power from somewhere else or something else. Shadow occultists / necromancers.<br /> <br /> 3) Magic you can gain through learning. Blue book rituals like summoning or warding.<br /> <br /> 4) Magic of things. The use of magical items or magic within items. Alchemy, mementos, etc.\u200b </div> </div> </div>1 and 4 i am excluding for the sake of simplicity. Characters which are born or changed a certain way are no longer Mortal, and magic items deserve their own comprehensive list.<br /> <br /> 2 and 3 are good, though some Geist ceremonies fall into the category of things you can just learn to do (like the passing on ceremony).<br /> <br /> Blood Sorcery (Sons of Phobos)\u2020, Shadow Rites (Shadow Occultists), Necromancy*, <s>goblin magic</s>** - all draw on other powers.<br /> <br /> Sorcery, Alchemy (Promethean type), i am not sure. I was thinking of Sorcery as being intrinsic manipulation, rather than drawing on power from Duat... I haven't read Promethean at all.<br /> <br /> Thaumatergy, Blue book rituals, Geist ceremonies, all fit into the manipulate the world on your own.<br /> <br /> Endowments i suspect can be either, but i haven't read anything about either...<br /> <br /> *Necromancy, as described in setting by Sin-eaters, exploits the power of the dead/Underworld, contrasted with ceremonies performed by regular folks to help which a Sin-eater would not call Necromancy.<br /> <br /> **I am actually going to exclude interactions with the Wyrd as not part of the Fallen world. Same with Supernal Magic. Though this is rather arbitrary. Don't @ me, the Hedge is not like the other Ephemeral realms. In fact iirc even the god-machine struggles to find ways of spreading infrastructure there.<br /> <br /> \u2020the sons of phobos draw power from stolen hearts/vitae without becoming vampires (like no Beast/Strix involvement) and it feels very much an edge case between just altering the world and drawing power from the magical blood which they have made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T03:27:31-07:00","id":1521115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521106#post1521106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Occultist (made up of it's two merits) is a separate thing to Rites. Shadow Occultists can use spirit Influences. Again, detailed in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon.<br /> The Pack is the book that allows humans to form a pack without Werewolves and use (&quot;Shadow&quot;?) Rites, limited to Open and Pack as per the norm, etc, with a different merit.<br /> <br /> Given that Promethean style Alchemy requires Pyros if not vitrol, I'm going with type 2 from the above list.<br /> <br /> Endowments can be any of the 4 flavours listed above, hypothetically. Lucifuge's Castigation is type 1, MalleusMaleficarum's Benedictions are type 2 [unless something is really wrong] and Aegis Kai Doru (AKD) uses Relics, a clear case for type 4.<br /> <br /> Type 3...of kind doesn't exist? <br /> Or rather, it isn't so much magic, as the rules for magic.<br /> <br /> Blue Book Summoning isn't actually calling an ephemeral entity and forcing it to come to you; it creates the Open condition and drops a bunch of resonant Essence because you put in the work to change the environment; like providing a birdhouse with a feeder. Exorcisms require the use of Bane material and knowledge of it's Ban...which would harm the entity and might well call on an instinctual revulsion. Abjuration might as well be a &quot;Beware of Large Dogs&quot; sign with actual wolves visible.<br /> The Blue Books don't have magic in them anymore. Just arcane physics.<br /> <br /> This is why I let things like the Hardened Exorcist merit, Ritual Mastery, that one tactic and that one Benediction stack on a roll...they aren't actually interacting with one another. Just the basic elements of the ephemerals nature.<br /> <br /> That said, while Ritual Sorcery does call upon Duat for some of it's abilities...this might be like the Insatiable Alchemists. We see those Duat based rituals more often, because the people we interact with have that perspective. The Arisen and the people they interact with are more likely to have ties to Duat.<br /> Certainly a closer reading reminds me that technically it manipulates the Sekhem on Earth to produce the effect...and Duat is defined by a lack of Sekhem (and comfort/mercy).<br /> <br /> So Ritual Sorcey might well be the closest thing we have to type 3 magic in the CoD universe...depending on the individual ritual. Kind of like what the God-Machine Infrastructure. It is making use of what is already there. <br /> <br /> I love how messy the metaphysics are but it can be confusing...and that is before unreliable narrator kicks in.<br /> <br /> For the record, the fact that the Sons of Phobos needed an initial outside source puts them (at least partially) in category 2 for me. It wasn't their blood. <br /> <br /> Of course, by this logic, Awakened spellcasting is type 2. You are imposing/drawing upon the laws of different reality and shoving them into the one you inhabit. Not a change, but worth pointing out.<br /> <br /> Ironically, this does strengthen the argument that what causes the Divergence for Deviants is type 3...even if the process makes them ineligible for this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T03:57:27-07:00","id":1521118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521115#post1521115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadow Occultist (made up of it's two merits) is a separate thing to Rites. Shadow Occultists can use spirit Influences. Again, detailed in Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon.<br /> The Pack is the book that allows humans to form a pack without Werewolves and use (&quot;Shadow&quot;?) Rites, limited to Open and Pack as per the norm, etc, with a different merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, adding the Pack to my list of things to read.<br /> <br /> But also, one of the benefits of the Shadow Occultist merit is that they can learn and lead pack rites without a pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Blue Books don't have magic in them anymore. Just arcane physics. </div> </div> </div>That seems like exactly the type of thing I want. Arcane physics\u2020 that anyone can do, as the lowest level/easiest to learn - no merits required? No special initiation beyond doing some research, and learning the basics of how the world works.<br /> <br /> These might be where a lot of Occultists start out. Before going on to look for more power - like they would derive from the Son's of Phobos (eating a heart) or the patronage of a shadow spirit (though this merit could also be generalised to Goetia and Ghost, possibly even G-M angels).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certainly a closer reading reminds me that technically it manipulates the Sekhem on Earth to produce the effect... </div> </div> </div>I do want to integrate this kind of manipulation into an advanced Arcane Physics. Even have thoughts about homebrewing the G-M as a creation of the Iremite Empire... But that is another story/potential history of the G-M option. I am not sure how much I would need to change to actually make Demon and Mummy powers cross over seamlessly. That isn't the main aim of this discussion...<br /> <br /> How is 'manipulating the Sekhem on Earth' different from arcane physics in your mind?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ironically, this does strengthen the argument that what causes the Divergence for Deviants is type 3...even if the process makes them ineligible for this discussion. </div> </div> </div>I would totally be happy to include Deviants in the discussion, as much as any Human can do the required twisting of their souls to gain the shadow Occultist merit\u2021, any human can be transformed into a Deviant. And that underlying type 3 occult forces in the world is interesting.<br /> <br /> But alas I have not read Deviant and don't currently intend to (finishing Demon, Mummy, Geist and Changeling are higher on my priority list...). My limited understanding is that they don't become 'magic', more like super heroes... And that would thematically limit them more than anything else\u2605<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2020i think that the God-machine operates on advanced Arcane Physics principles.<br /> <br /> \u2021and that reminds me, i must look into how the Purified and Shadow Occultist initiation differ/share similarities. Because bith end up making you closer to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> \u2605Also with powers derived from the shape of their souls, are Deviants like Awakened mages using legacy attainments? I guess you could expand Mage Legacies to i Clyde mortal members who have their souls shaped to perform certain 'miracles'... that would be type 3.<br /> <br /> EDIT: i thought of this too<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Ritual Sorcey might well be the closest thing we have to type 3 magic in the CoD universe...depending on the individual ritual. </div> </div> </div>I think certain Geist ceremonies qualify here too. Though I am thinking of all 'arcane physics' as you put it as magic.. certain ceremonies do involve drawing power from the Underworld, but other don't involve it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added a note on ceremonies. 08-21-2023, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T05:41:54-07:00","id":1521123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521118#post1521118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like exactly the type of thing I want. Arcane physics\u2020 that anyone can do, as the lowest level/easiest to learn - no merits required? No special initiation beyond doing some research, and learning the basics of how the world works.<br /> \u200b<br /> *snip*<br /> <br /> \u2020i think that the God-machine operates on advanced Arcane Physics principles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, my choice of language there was intentional <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521118#post1521118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> \u2605Also with powers derived from the shape of their souls, are Deviants like Awakened mages using legacy attainments? I guess you could expand Mage Legacies to i Clyde mortal members who have their souls shaped to perform certain 'miracles'... that would be type 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulating people's souls is a good way for them to stop counting as 'mortal humans'. There is a reason why Sin-Eaters can't use Ritual Sorcery. Not saying that won't work. It is kind of how Mummy's Affinities work, so technically yes, the theory is sound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521118#post1521118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> EDIT: i thought of this too<br /> <br /> I think certain Geist ceremonies qualify here too. Though I am thinking of all 'arcane physics' as you put it as magic.. certain ceremonies do involve drawing power from the Underworld, but other don't involve it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but like Ritual Sorcery, Ceremonies are merits. So that is a thing, if you really want to hold on to that limitation.<br /> It should be noted that the Ritual Sorcerer merit creates &quot;slots&quot; for rituals to be learned, so this gets close to the &quot;research and learn&quot; kind of magic.<br /> <br /> That said, only the 5 base Blue Book fit the strictest definition of what you are looking for:<ul><li>Summoning</li> <li>Exorcism (inverse Summoning)</li> <li>Abjuration (Exorcism on an area)</li> <li>Warding/Binding</li> </ul>The bit that gets me, every one of these &quot;magic rites&quot; are individual to the entity they are affecting, at least according to RAW.<br /> I'd tend to rule a tad more lenient than that; any ephemeral entity of the same category, rank and general influence is a valid target. This also applies to other logical extrapolation, such as Open Rite Mastery for Ritual Sorcerers Appling the relevant bonuses to all &quot;base rites&quot; of that type. Which is NOT how it works by RAW, as again; every Exorcism, Summoning, Abjuration, Warding and Binding for every entity is technically a unique working.<br /> <br /> That I have heard of others on the forum using the &quot;Building Equipment&quot; rules (pg 100, Chronicles of Darkness) with the Occult skill to create &quot;talismans&quot;. They follow the same rules, providing a bonus to certain Skills, but look different. Just work by magic, but are not magical enough to trigger any mechanical advantage over mundane equipment. No hitting Amkhata with one of these &quot;talismans&quot; for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T06:32:08-07:00","id":1521126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521123#post1521123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The bit that gets me, every one of these &quot;magic rites&quot; are individual to the entity they are affecting, at least according to RAW.<br /> I'd tend to rule a tad more lenient than that; any ephemeral entity of the same category, rank and general influence is a valid target.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad it wasn't just me that was bothered by that. Second Sight: Third Eye has a solution to it for warding, which IMO is the biggest offender of the group in being &quot;single creature only&quot;. I don't mind summonings, bindings, and exorcisms being creature specific but warding really bothered me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T06:43:28-07:00","id":1521127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521123#post1521123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, my choice of language there was intentional <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Manipulating people's souls is a good way for them to stop counting as 'mortal humans'. There is a reason why Sin-Eaters can't use Ritual Sorcery. Not saying that won't work. It is kind of how Mummy's Affinities work, so technically yes, the theory is sound.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps, but like Ritual Sorcery, Ceremonies are merits. So that is a thing, if you really want to hold on to that limitation.<br /> It should be noted that the Ritual Sorcerer merit creates &quot;slots&quot; for rituals to be learned, so this gets close to the &quot;research and learn&quot; kind of magic.<br /> <br /> That said, only the 5 base Blue Book fit the strictest definition of what you are looking for:<ul><li>Summoning</li> <li>Exorcism (inverse Summoning)</li> <li>Abjuration (Exorcism on an area)</li> <li>Warding/Binding</li> </ul>The bit that gets me, every one of these &quot;magic rites&quot; are individual to the entity they are affecting, at least according to RAW.<br /> I'd tend to rule a tad more lenient than that; any ephemeral entity of the same category, rank and general influence is a valid target. This also applies to other logical extrapolation, such as Open Rite Mastery for Ritual Sorcerers Appling the relevant bonuses to all &quot;base rites&quot; of that type. Which is NOT how it works by RAW, as again; every Exorcism, Summoning, Abjuration, Warding and Binding for every entity is technically a unique working.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure, just re-reading a few bits, and it seems Geist claims the blue book magic are just ceremonies that have become so commonly known you don't need to buy them as merits.<br /> <br /> While Mummy has each as an Open Rite.<br /> <br /> Open rite mastery is where you get Mummy merits to benefit you.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what they mean by 'each individual interaction is a seperate open rite'<br /> <br /> Your take is that they mean an individual ghost being abjured is one open rite? And if you want to bind the same ghost that is a seperate rite. But also binding another ghost would be a third rite, and binding a spirit of fire a fourth... That is extremely limiting given the number of Open Rite masteries you can have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That I have heard of others on the forum using the &quot;Building Equipment&quot; rules (pg 100, Chronicles of Darkness) with the Occult skill to create &quot;talismans&quot;. They follow the same rules, providing a bonus to certain Skills, but look different. Just work by magic, but are not magical enough to trigger any mechanical advantage over mundane equipment. No hitting Amkhata with one of these &quot;talismans&quot; for example. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i dislike the use of the building equipment rules for this. It feels rather cheap somehow, in fact it reminds me of other game systems where the magic system just uses the normal mechanics with what feels like a 'magical flavour'... i did not buy that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T07:56:07-07:00","id":1521130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521127#post1521127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what they mean by 'each individual interaction is a seperate open rite'<br /> <br /> Your take is that they mean an individual ghost being abjured is one open rite? And if you want to bind the same ghost that is a seperate rite. But also binding another ghost would be a third rite, and binding a spirit of fire a fourth... That is extremely limiting given the number of Open Rite masteries you can have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly they're conflating &quot;the summoning ritual for each individual fiend is a separate Open Rite&quot; and &quot;summoning and warding ephemeral entities involves creating or removing the Conditions they use to Manifest or leveraging their Banes, which vary by entity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given the comparative simplicity of lower-Rank entities, it seems reasonable that commonly-available methods that don't require special qualities, training, or resources can't provide a global ward against all spirits/ghosts/etc; that's the domain of dedicated supernatural powers and projects, whereas it's relatively straightforward to ward against an entire species of firebugs that roam an area due to shared metaphysical flaws.<br /> <br /> Also I need to point out that an Open Rite Mastery just gives you bonuses when performing an Open Rite; &quot;these things are Open Rites&quot; is otherwise literally the same thing as Geist saying &quot;these are functionally Ceremonies so common that they don't have a dot rating,&quot; so there's little practical difference between creating the Anchor Condition for a fallen soldier and doing so for a victim of famine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T10:30:20-07:00","id":1521137,"title":"","content":"Back to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> I presume Wolf rites require that you be a Werewolf (or wolf-blooded with a tell?), But Pack rites just require a pack?<br /> <br /> And what defines a Pack is their Totem Spirit (which i think the Dark Eras book said could be a Geist or other Underworld entity, similar to how changeling court can have other powerful entities as their patron).<br /> <br /> Likewise Shadow Occultists have a patron spirit <s>manipulating</s> granting them essence etc. And they are able to perform Pack rites.<br /> <br /> Could this be generalised? How would a Pack/Krewe/Motley* function with only 'arcane physics' binding them? And a Totem/Patron entity empowering them (maybe not pack rites if it isn't a Spirit as the Patron?)<br /> <br /> Some obviously a Mummy's Cult would use their Mummy as the Patron. But I haven't read too much about the power Mummys tend to invest in their Cults.<br /> <br /> I think this would be a category 2 group, with generalised rules based on Packs formed of humans (with category 3 group like a Krewe/Mystery Cult follow some creed and sharing ceremonies as a seperate thing).<br /> <br /> *I think Motleys can include non-Changelings in their pledges, but I'm not sure what benefits they get that aren't Wyrd powered. And I am excluding the Wyrd from 'arcane physics'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  typos 08-21-2023, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T11:31:14-07:00","id":1521138,"title":"","content":"Wolf rites are, theoretically, werewolf only, while pack rites are open to wolf blooded, shadow occultists, and I believe there's several others that can perform them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T12:35:30-07:00","id":1521140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521138#post1521138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf rites are, theoretically, werewolf only, while pack rites are open to wolf blooded, shadow occultists, and I believe there's several others that can perform them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, i was wrong about wolf-blooded, only some of them can lead a pack rite (depending on tells) not wolf rites.<br /> <br /> And there are rumours of human cults/packs doing pack rites with claimed taking the position of the werewolves. Which is an interesting plot hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T12:55:14-07:00","id":1521143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521140#post1521140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yes, i was wrong about wolf-blooded, only some of them can lead a pack rite (depending on tells) not wolf rites.<br /> <br /> And there are rumours of human cults/packs doing pack rites with claimed taking the position of the werewolves. Which is an interesting plot hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I recalled there being some other example where something led wolf rites but I couldn't remember fully. <br /> <br /> And it really is an interesting plot hook, I think the claimed are awesome villains, maybe some of the best in CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T15:56:49-07:00","id":1521154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521127#post1521127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what they mean by 'each individual interaction is a seperate open rite'<br /> <br /> Your take is that they mean an individual ghost being abjured is one open rite? And if you want to bind the same ghost that is a seperate rite. But also binding another ghost would be a third rite, and binding a spirit of fire a fourth... That is extremely limiting given the number of Open Rite masteries you can have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay this is going to be a tad painful but I'll try. Let start with the easy one.<br /> Every Exorcism 'rite' is unique to each individual ghost, spirit, angel and every ephemeral entity. It requires researching each and every time.<br /> This applies to the other blur book rites too.<br /> You don't use an Abjuration on ghosts; you use it on Old Tom. <br /> You don't Ward against disease spirit; You Ward against Blood-Upon-Your-Breath.<br /> <br /> Upon checking, this might be a carryover from 1st edition. I did not find the exact passage before I had to leave for work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T10:01:45-07:00","id":1521198,"title":"","content":"Looking at the blue book, summoning and warding/binding require specific knowledge of the thing you're trying to summon or drive away. When Summoning you need to get the conditions (and Conditions) right to allow the thing to manifest, whether that means getting a specific ghost's Anchor or causing your summoning area to become Resonant with a particular spirit. <br /> Abjuration looks more general though, since it works the same without regard for specific Bans or Banes. Warding/Binding combines Abjuration with the specific bane of an entity to protect a specified are, so that's also specific to particular entities, or at least to entities with the same Bane, since the book calls out low-Rank ghosts having a Bane of salt quite often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T14:15:57-07:00","id":1521279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521198#post1521198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the blue book, summoning and warding/binding require specific knowledge of the thing you're trying to summon or drive away. When Summoning you need to get the conditions (and Conditions) right to allow the thing to manifest, whether that means getting a specific ghost's Anchor or causing your summoning area to become Resonant with a particular spirit.<br /> Abjuration looks more general though, since it works the same without regard for specific Bans or Banes. Warding/Binding combines Abjuration with the specific bane of an entity to protect a specified are, so that's also specific to particular entities, or at least to entities with the same Bane, since the book calls out low-Rank ghosts having a Bane of salt quite often.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the Blue book, but could it not be the same basic ritual, but each one uses the bane of the entity for the procedure... Thus you still have to research the subject, but if someone just tells you the bane then you will be able to use it?<br /> <br /> Or is this the bane and the ban used together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T18:46:49-07:00","id":1521304,"title":"","content":"As far as the blue book is concerned, the actual ritual matters way less than knowing and using the bans and banes and summoning conditions of the entity you're interacting with.<br /> Based on the blue book and interpreting the Mummy sorcery mechanics strictly I'd say that Abjuration in general could be one Open Rite, but summoning and warding/binding would count as open rites per unique set of banes and summoning conditions. And &quot;classic exorcism&quot; is called out as a combination of Binding to keep an entity in place, Abjuration to provide a spiritual kick, and using Bans and Banes together as much as possible.<br /> Spirits likely have different enough conditions that I'd say every spirit is unique, but IIRC every ghost has their body as an anchor, so I could see an argument for &quot;summoning any ghost with their bones&quot; could count as an Open Rite if you wanted it to, and enough ghosts have salt as a bane that &quot;warding a ghost away with salt&quot; could also be pretty generally useful. If you want to summon a particular ghost out of the Underworld, though, I'd probably make that an Open Rite per individual ghost, similar to summoning particular fiends out of Duat.<br /> <br /> My reading of the Sorcerer rules is that you only use up a Rite slot with an Open Rite if you choose to Master it. So if you're summoning and banishing lots of ghosts or spirits that are just hanging around in Nefer-Khertet/twilight then I think you just do that with the blue book mechanics, minimal as they are, and treat it as an unmastered open rite, and save the Mastery for striking up a relationship with a particular ghost or spirit that you summon on a regular basis.<br /> So given that Sorcerers aren't really supposed to know a ton of Rites to begin with and that anyone can do an Open Rite, and that you're supposed to do the the rite the exact same way every time and the name of the being you're summoning is probably part of it, I personally would err on the side of making each type of interaction with a specific entity it's own Open Rite, and just using the blue book rules for them when applicable. If a sorcerer wanted to Master a particular rite, that's kind of like spending xp on an Ally, where they're deepening a relationship with a particular ghost or spirit.<br /> That's just me, though. If you want Sorcerers in your game to benefit as much as possible from Open Rite Mastery you can interpret the mechanics as liberally as you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T20:52:15-07:00","id":1521309,"title":"","content":"One interesting question, would you say mortal magic needs to be mortal only? I have been reading up on binding, abjuration, etc and it seems that a common interpretation is that you don't have to be mortal to use them. It seems that humanity at the least serves as an equivalent to integrity and so nothing prevents vampires from using blue book magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T09:42:14-07:00","id":1521332,"title":"","content":"I just did a quick spot-check on a number of core rulebooks and was surprised that the summoning/exorcism/warding rules generally weren't there; just the Manifestation flowchart and even that wasn't in every book I don't think.<br /> I think it's clear that nothing stops any intelligent entity from leveraging Bans, Banes and Manifestation conditions to interact with ephemeral entities in general, but for me Abjuration is a sticking point since it talks about using the power of a human soul. Most of the player splats have souls, but they've usually been altered in some way. I think my own interpretation is that if you can't buy Mortal-only Supernatural Merits, you can't do an Abjuration blue-book style, you'd need to leverage your other powers. It just feels like a simpler rule-of-thumb than making a bunch of judgement calls about which PC splats have souls that work that way and which don't.<br /> Although if I was doing a chronicle in which, for example, PC Changelings were interacting a great deal with ghosts or spirits and none of them had powers that helped with that I'd probably re-think that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T10:07:58-07:00","id":1521335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521309#post1521309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One interesting question, would you say mortal magic needs to be mortal only? I have been reading up on binding, abjuration, etc and it seems that a common interpretation is that you don't have to be mortal to use them. It seems that humanity at the least serves as an equivalent to integrity and so nothing prevents vampires from using blue book magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>My baseline is no.<br /> <br /> Can it be mortal only magics, sure.<br /> Does it have to be? No.<br /> <br /> The reverse case it Blood magic (sorcery that kindred do with vitae) - the Sons of Phobos have demonstrated a way around only kindred having access to this by developing their own ritual. So i would have assumed it was Kindred only, but now I think anyone can do it...<br /> <br /> There may be a subset of mortal only magics, as Nikokk discussed above. I just want a comprehensive list of thing all mortals can do (with enough effort/the right contacts).<br /> <br /> Of course if only mortals can do abjuration, where does that leave sin-eaters (lacking a soul, but dealing with ghosts all the time)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  fixing error in my question. 08-24-2023, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T10:15:44-07:00","id":1521337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521335#post1521335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course if only mortals can do abjuration, where does that leave sin-eaters (lacking a soul, but dealing with ghosts all the time)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I came across a sin-eaters reference while I was reading those posts. Sin Eaters apparently treat abjuration etc as ceremonies and ceremonies are open to anyone to perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T11:22:39-07:00","id":1521342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521337#post1521337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I came across a sin-eaters reference while I was reading those posts. Sin Eaters apparently treat abjuration etc as ceremonies and ceremonies are open to anyone to perform.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point actually. Looking just at the Chronicles of Darkness book I'd said Abjuration felt like a mortal-only thing, but it's also equated with both Ceremonies in Geist and Open Rites in Mummy, both of which can be &quot;done by anyone&quot; in contexts that include other supernatural beings. I'm <i>pretty sure</i> Mummies can't create Vestiges by themselves, though, and that's also labelled as an Open Rite, but that's a Mummy-specific exception.<br /> Anyway, that resolves the issue of whether sin-eaters can do Abjuration (yes, as a Ceremony), but they have enough other powers dealing with ghosts that I'd be surprised if Abjuration is the best tool for them outside of niche circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T08:47:30-07:00","id":1521665,"title":"","content":"Looking more at shadow cults:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/209092-werewolves-vs-demons?p=210996#post210996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &lt;snip&gt; Rat Host can't be trusted.<br /> <br /> The Pure do allow spirits to run the show, get mounts, claim people and form cults. Tearing down the gauntlet? maybe when they're numerous enough and can wage war upon humanity and &quot;teach it its proper place&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bif this is still accurate, how would Pure Werewolves feel about Shaodw Occultists? About a more even arrangement of power? Or Purified (who might form a more human-centric Shadow Cult)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T09:11:26-07:00","id":1521668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521665#post1521665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking more at shadow cults:<br /> <br /> \u200bif this is still accurate, how would Pure Werewolves feel about Shaodw Occultists? About a more even arrangement of power? Or Purified (who might form a more human-centric Shadow Cult)?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general thing, the Pure believe that what spirits choose to do isn't the Pure's problem. If a bunch of spirits want to get together and form a cult the Pure as a whole probably generally don't care. But then it comes down to the individuals involved. Is one of the Pure a former cultist who was rescued from a cult in their childhood? They may not take kindly to the spirits forming one. Or maybe one of the Pure has a cousin who has been claimed by a spirit involved with the cult, that could be a problem. Or if the cult is competing with the Pure pack for any given resource / hunting grounds, that could be a source of conflict. <br /> <br /> As to the Purified, there's less guidance going across games, but I think it's largely going to be in the same theme as the above, not our problem. <br /> <br /> It is worth noting though, the Pure are more likely to have spirit allies than the Forsaken and as such are more likely to be dragged into drama in the spirit world involving stuff like this than it might seem at the onset. It's entirely possible that the Flame Touched are friendly with a group of spirits who do have a problem with spirit cultists, or heck, even have a problem with a human who thinks to transform himself into a spirit. Spirits are individuals to, after all. <br /> <br /> So ya, a Pure / Purified / Shadow Occultist alliance could work, or they could all be at each other's throats. It wouldn't be entirely unreasonable for it to be both situations at the same time. Maybe one pack of Pure is backing a Purified lead group of Shadow Occultists in another area as a weapon to use against the Forsaken while another pack of Pure has various reasons to oppose that group. Bonus points if the packs are legitimately friendly with one another. <br /> <br /> One other thing you might consider, an individual ghost would tyrant might well have shadow occultists in their pack, and may even be friendly with a member of the Purified, after all the stories of the ancient city of Sumer and the Uratha ruling over humans have to come from somewhere and an immortal seeking to manipulate a lone wolf would be a wonderful source for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T16:31:43-07:00","id":1521790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521342#post1521342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point actually. Looking just at the Chronicles of Darkness book I'd said Abjuration felt like a mortal-only thing, but it's also equated with both Ceremonies in Geist and Open Rites in Mummy, both of which can be &quot;done by anyone&quot; in contexts that include other supernatural beings. I'm <i>pretty sure</i> Mummies can't create Vestiges by themselves, though, and that's also labelled as an Open Rite, but that's a Mummy-specific exception.<br /> Anyway, that resolves the issue of whether sin-eaters can do Abjuration (yes, as a Ceremony), but they have enough other powers dealing with ghosts that I'd be surprised if Abjuration is the best tool for them outside of niche circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say that mortal interaction seems like a great thing for splats that lack interaction with the ephemeral. Where humanity is easy to sub in for integrity I do struggle with thinking how demon best would interact as cover isn't an equivalent trait. Even though some parts of demon, for example boltholes, seem to suggest they should be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T10:21:47-07:00","id":1521819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521790#post1521790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will say that mortal interaction seems like a great thing for splats that lack interaction with the ephemeral. Where humanity is easy to sub in for integrity I do struggle with thinking how demon best would interact as cover isn't an equivalent trait. Even though some parts of demon, for example boltholes, seem to suggest they should be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, Abjuration is just an opposed roll that uses a character's Resolve + Composure, which every major splat has. Virtue and high Integrity can give bonuses to the roll, and vice versa Vice and low Integrity can give negatives. So, certain splat traits like Cover or Harmony or even Satiety that don't really map to Integrity that well are a bit awkward, thematically, but you could keep Abjurations available but just not hand out those bonuses. If you're including Abjuration in your game because you want more options to interact with ephemeral entities for your players I'd just handwave it and say that whatever they've got is close enough to a soul to work.<br /> <br /> As for mortals, I don't remember if anyone's brought it up explicitly, but summoning alone can power an entire magic system for a game. Most ephemeral entities have some kind of power, so summon something and then convince or compel it to use its powers on your behalf. Spend time researching previous occultists efforts to learn names, summoning conditions, pre-existing agreements, etc. Mortal sorcerers from Mummy can summon and control Amhkhata and fiends from Duat, which further expand your options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 09-01-2023, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T13:37:35-07:00","id":1521834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521819#post1521819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;<br /> As for mortals, I don't remember if anyone's brought it up explicitly, but summoning alone can power an entire magic system for a game. Most ephemeral entities have some kind of power, so summon something and then convince or compel it to use its powers on your behalf. Spend time researching previous occultists efforts to learn names, summoning conditions, pre-existing agreements, etc. Mortal sorcerers from Mummy can summon and control Amhkhata and fiends from Duat, which further expand your options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, some of the ceremonies from Geist would cover summoning ghost (or other more dangerous deathly entities). And the binding/Compelling them bit.<br /> <br /> Similar rules should exist for spirits.<br /> <br /> And calling these ritual Necromancy and Shamanism for flavour is fine.<br /> <br /> Summoning other things is likely less common, goetia need a iris to pass through and they are typically rarer than (say) places to cross the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Supernal beings require a connection to the supernal (or maybe just a natural verge). And Abyssal entities may require an Abyssal verge.<br /> <br /> The Strix can probably be summoned, but bidning them likely requires some trickery and sunlight.<br /> <br /> Infernalists of all stripes likely summon entities from various hell dimensions desperate to strike a deal and take a soul... Or otherwise mess you up.<br /> <br /> And summoners recommended even stranger things...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T14:53:30-07:00","id":1521838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521834#post1521834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal beings require a connection to the supernal (or maybe just a natural verge).</div> </div> </div> </div>Summoning Supernal beings requires a Path and three dots in an Arcanum. Closest you're getting without being a mage is being extremely lucky re: what its Ban is unless a plot device is involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T20:50:27-07:00","id":1521853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521834#post1521834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, some of the ceremonies from Geist would cover summoning ghost (or other more dangerous deathly entities). And the binding/Compelling them bit.<br /> <br /> Similar rules should exist for spirits.<br /> <br /> And calling these ritual Necromancy and Shamanism for flavour is fine.<br /> <br /> Summoning other things is likely less common, goetia need a iris to pass through and they are typically rarer than (say) places to cross the gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Supernal beings require a connection to the supernal (or maybe just a natural verge). And Abyssal entities may require an Abyssal verge.<br /> <br /> The Strix can probably be summoned, but bidning them likely requires some trickery and sunlight.<br /> <br /> Infernalists of all stripes likely summon entities from various hell dimensions desperate to strike a deal and take a soul... Or otherwise mess you up.<br /> <br /> And summoners recommended even stranger things...</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't necessarily have to compel ephemeral entities with other magic; if they're sentient and able to communicate you can bribe them, leverage their Ban or Bane, or maybe use the Chronicles of Darkness conversation system to strike a deal with them, or just roleplay it. If you take the core gameplay mechanic for getting your summons to do what you want to be talking to them, you can build some open rites or ceremonies or whatever to support that rather than building a ton of rituals to try to cover everything.<br /> This would be <i>dangerous</i>, a lot of the time, at least without a lot of prep and research, but that's part of the fun. I'd lean towards having mortal occultists build relationships with a handful of ephemeral entities of whatever kind, getting to know them, summoning them to trade favors with, building trust, or trying to assert dominance. You can help keep a ghost around and strong by helping preserve their memory, shepherd some kind of spirit in Twilight by keeping the Resonant condition active somewhere, maintain some Infrastructure for an angel, etc. With a decent Occult skill you should be able to research these kinds of activities from previous generations of practical occultists as well; giving your characters some idea how to do it, survive it, mistakes to avoid, and maybe some names, bans, banes, and anchors or whatever to get them started.<br /> In addition to the usual suspects, the CoD corebook has a little sidebar about building your own kind of ephemeral entities; you basically just have to decide what rules they follow and which they put their own spin on. So if you wanted to create, like, elemental spirits, or djinn, or gremlins or something you can do that too if you want to give mortal occultists more options for summoning that don't quite follow the existing rules for spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T20:59:37-07:00","id":1521854,"title":"","content":"To back track onto the bit that I missed; I would add the Pure aren't a monolith and would have different reactions as a trend along tribal lines on top of individuals that vary by circumstances.<br /> Predator kings would probably react less well to Shadow Occultists and Purified than a Fire Touched as an example stereotype.<br /> <br /> Heck, a Purified practically is a spirit to a degree (Rank, Essence, etc), so they would probably get better treatment from the Pure across the board, than a Shadow Occultist. Unless a human truing into a spirit is seen as some kind of heresy. Which it absolutely might. The Purified get and can use the first two tiers of Word of Dead Dominion Utterance applied to spirits, not ghosts as a default ability. So they can (forcibly) summon spirits and give them commands; the Utterance doesn't give them a roll to resist, but I'd assume it would be the Purified's Rank + Power vs their Rank + Resistance but that is me house ruling that spirits even get one. Ghosts don't when Arisen do this. This is on top of the Dread powers and/or Numina they get. They got buffed in 2e/Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, the Purified are the Immortals that are furthest from Mummy the Curse in nature. They are also the ones I'd argue cannot use Ritual Sorcery or Necromantic Ceremonies, in contrast to every other playable Immortal, including Visitors. Don't get me wrong, I like the Purified, but they are not human anymore. They are certainly powerful enough that a Pack of werewolves would ignore them if they are doing anything of consequence in the Shadow.<br /> If not for their lack of Influence, I'd argue that could be a Patron for Shadow Occultists...and I'd be willing to let Purified be Shadow Occultist, if not for their ability to issue commands to spirits.<br /> <br /> On the Ides of other ephemeral entities to summon, Mummy the Curse lets you summon Fiends which are like Amkhata on steroids and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Inferno\" target=\"_blank\">Inferno </a>does outline a few subvarieties of ephemerals that H:tV implies still exist. Heck the Maeljin in Shunned by the Moon qualify and give out special boons in 2e besides! <br /> <br /> Has anyone mentioned the Skinchanger merit in Dark Eras yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-02-2023, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T03:54:40-07:00","id":1521867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521838#post1521838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summoning Supernal beings requires a Path and three dots in an Arcanum. Closest you're getting without being a mage is being extremely lucky re: what its Ban is unless a plot device is involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i think most starting (mage) characters have that requirement... I didn't realise you needed 3 dots in the primary aswell, thought that was only for the attainment (which seems really weak, but that is a seperate question entirely).<br /> <br /> That said, don't you usually get a supernal being who wants to be summoned? Thus if you go to a verge and just do a ritual (with the right research and appropriate symbols) a supernal being can just show up on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can help keep a ghost around and strong by helping preserve their memory, shepherd some kind of spirit in Twilight by keeping the Resonant condition active somewhere, maintain some Infrastructure for an angel, etc. </div> </div> </div>I like that, Shadow Occultists in particular do something like this, excepting the condition is that they are open for possession to the spirit, so it is just a little bit more extreme (and desirable to get a higher rank spirit perhaps).<br /> <br /> And I think Angels might be less interested in deals since they have missions and lack freewill, though I think there are angels which haven't quite fallen but aren't exactly on task (Exiles?) So maybe.<br /> <br /> Ghosts in the other hand have everything to gain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just to be clear, the Purified are the Immortals that are furthest from Mummy the Curse in nature. </div> </div> </div>Honestly i think the Purified are closer to werewolves (part-spirit/part-flesh) than to any other entity... But yeah, they are more like spirits (with essence, access to numina and influences in 1e).<br /> <br /> But I would agree with you somewhat on them not being able to do Open rites, though I think that is like saying a Mage can't do Open Rites... Not necessary. A Mage doing an Open Rite is likely seriously handicapping themself (though getting around paradox might make it worthwhile - the same drawbacks don't apply to 'spirit magic')<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are certainly powerful enough that a Pack of werewolves would ignore them if they are doing anything of consequence in the Shadow. If not for their lack of Influence, I'd argue that could be a Patron for Shadow Occultists...and I'd be willing to let Purified be Shadow Occultist, if not for their ability to issue commands to spirits. </div> </div> </div>Presumably that means they could join a pack, or with sufficient power/rank create a pack (ie act as a pack totem).<br /> <br /> Not sure how werewolves in general would view that.<br /> <br /> Patronizing Shadow Occultists is fine, but i don't think they can become one. Eating the ephemeral of a spirit is likely just going to give them essence to their essence pool, if the resonance is off it should have similar effects to any Spirit eating incompatible essence... Joining and helping Shadow Occultists in a ritual is a different matter. But I think Shadow Occultists becoming a Purified seems more likely (though the requisite loss of integrity may make this more difficult).<br /> <br /> Where are fiends listed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":"autocarroted) 09-02-2023, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T05:16:44-07:00","id":1521869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521867#post1521867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*<br /> Honestly i think the Purified are closer to werewolves (part-spirit/part-flesh) than to any other entity... But yeah, they are more like spirits (with essence, access to numina and influences in 1e).<br /> <br /> But I would agree with you somewhat on them not being able to do Open rites, though I think that is like saying a Mage can't do Open Rites... Not necessary. A Mage doing an Open Rite is likely seriously handicapping themself (though getting around paradox might make it worthwhile - the same drawbacks don't apply to 'spirit magic')<br /> <br /> <br /> Presumably that means they could join a pack, or with sufficient power/rank create a pack (ie act as a pack totem).<br /> <br /> Not sure how werewolves in general would view that.<br /> <br /> Patronizing Shadow Occultists is fine, but i don't think they can become one. Eating the ephemeral of a spirit is likely just going to give them essence to their essence pool, if the resonance is off it should have similar effects to any Spirit eating incompatible essence... Joining and helping Shadow Occultists in a ritual is a different matter. But I think Shadow Occultists becoming a Purified seems more likely (though the requisite loss of integrity may make this more difficult).<br /> <br /> Where are friends listed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back, I must not have explained myself very clearly.<br /> While Open Rites are generally unnecessary for a Purified to deal with spirits, the other ephemerals (Ghosts, Angels, Quashmalim, Fiends?, Goetia, Shades, etc) are a different story.<br /> <br /> While the Purified can join a Pack (literally anyone can, nothing special required) being a Totem might be beyond them. Their 2e/CoD portrayal is buffed but they DO actually lack a fundamental part of being an ephemeral entity: no Influence dots. While this might not be a deal breaker...with only one exception even alluded to (an Arisen) all the Totems, even the weird ones, mentioned in 2e/CoD are the traditional 3 ephemeral entities with Influences. Admittedly none of them have been officially stated out, though I think Chris Allen did a Ghost Totem Pack on his Patreon.<br /> <br /> Werewolves do have odd reactions to weird Pack members; they cover most of the gameline protagonists in <i>The Pack. </i>I'd guess Purified would fit somewhere between a Mage and Spirit in terms of what reactions they would provoke.<br /> <br /> No-one mentioned eating spirits, though I guess it is another way Purified differ from spirits. They also can't harvest Essence form resonance, given that they don't have anything to resonant with.<br /> <br /> Shadow Occultists bargain with spirits for Patronage, which let's them use they're Patron's Influences. Think of Shadow Occultist's as having Lodge Sorcery; they follow a spirit's Ban and Bane in exchange for Essence and Influences. No Influences, not a potential Patron.<br /> As I said, if they Purified could not just tell the spirit to hand over the magic, I could see an argument that a Purified could bargain to use a spirit's Influence. Even if they have a larger Essence pool. With the Purified capable of just commanding the spirit to use the Influence on their behalf, I don't think they should be Shadow Occultists.<br /> <br /> Fiends are detailed in <i>Mummy: the Curse 2e</i> on pg 321 of that book. The part where I consider them more powerful than Amkhata has to do with the fact they follow ephemeral rules for manifestation, thus allowing them to bypass the need to devour Sekhem or mortals. That said, if they don't feed on enough Essence to keep up with their hourglass, they end up back in Duat. I used Fiend rules (using the appropriate components from <i>Book of Lasting Death</i>) to create Sha for my First Sothic Turn one-shot recently. I did slightly raise the Essence rating.<br /> I assume they called them Fiends, because the term &quot;demon&quot; was already loaded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-02-2023, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T06:25:43-07:00","id":1521871,"title":"","content":"By RAW there is nothing to stop a purified from performing sorcery, Mummy has a blanket statement that immortals can purchase sorcery and nothing in the Purified entry states otherwise.<br /> <br /> There is something else stopping a purified from being the patron of shadow occultists, Purified don't get manifestations. Without manifestations you cannot ride nor claim a human and being ridden or claimed is a requirement to gaining the shadow occultist merit. For that same reason I wouldn't allow them to become shadow occultists.<br /> <br /> I do think they could insert themselves into the cult on either the human or spirit side though, as a leader / advisor / boss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T09:02:50-07:00","id":1521879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521869#post1521869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No-one mentioned eating spirits, though I guess it is another way Purified differ from spirits. They also can't harvest Essence form resonance, given that they don't have anything to resonant with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have misremebered the becoming a Shadow Occultist process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadow Occultists bargain with spirits for Patronage, which let's them use they're Patron's Influences. </div> </div> </div>The Patron also makes them eat a 'bodily fluid' of ephemeral, in order for them to contain essence. Iirc eating a part of the spirit/eating some ephemera is required so not entirely the same as eating a spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think of Shadow Occultist's as having Lodge Sorcery; they follow a spirit's Ban and Bane in exchange for Essence and Influences. No Influences, not a potential Patron.<br /> As I said, if they Purified could not just tell the spirit to hand over the magic, I could see an argument that a Purified could bargain to use a spirit's Influence. Even if they have a larger Essence pool. With the Purified capable of just commanding the spirit to use the Influence on their behalf.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i am not sure how to place them, other than in the same definitely above Shadow Occultists, on par with werewolves and spirits (of equal rank) but i wonder where the least powerful mortal practitioner can reach.<br /> <br /> Like a Shaman who doesn't have an essence pool. Still envokes spirits, negotiated with them to use their influence for what they want. Actually reminds me of Exalted dealig with minor gods.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T09:03:54-07:00","id":1521880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1521867#post1521867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, don't you usually get a supernal being who wants to be summoned?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e does not say anything to this effect and 1e says the opposite is not uncommon in Summoners' section on The Dangers of Summoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T04:59:42-07:00","id":1522626,"title":"","content":"I feel the need to add here, leylines and nodes are only really mentioned in Mage (and a little bit tangentially in Mummy relating to the sacred geometry and Lifeweb) but they aren't connected directly to anything particularly supernal.<br /> <br /> They are speculated to bring some aspect of natural magic of the Fallen world. With a forces aligned node able to power simple electrical devices, while a matter aligned one can repair damage objects etc.<br /> <br /> I like to think sufficient occult research could uncover these principles and maybe even expand on them. That any mortal could tap into the power of leylines and the natural magic of the Fallen world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T11:19:08-07:00","id":1522636,"title":"","content":"I'd probably limit something like that to be a bit less powerful than the effects of the spell in question, but I could see someone with good enough sense of things getting a benefit from arranging things properly at a ley line nexus, sure.<br /> I'm reading China Mieville's Kraken right now, and there's a character in there who can fold up complicated machinery and living people and fit them in boxes that they shouldn't be able to fit in, and that don't weigh as much as they should, and they still work properly and can be unfolded without hurting them. That's his whole thing, it's the culmination of years of work on weird math disciplines and super advanced origami.<br /> Something like that could fit into Chronicles as a human who discovered some odd property the GM's occult physics, able to fold things in impossible ways into impossible spaces. Give them a custom-made supernatural Merit, kind of like City-Walking from the corebook, and you're golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T03:36:38-07:00","id":1522664,"title":"","content":"Yeah, i think low level background stuff with Leylines could be cool, combined with using them to help enhance appropriate rituals.<br /> <br /> The benefits in Mage are so minor, but also just about the only Fallen Magic thing that mages even both to mention (unless you count shaping the soul so they can do magic powered by their own soul rather than relying on the connection to the supernal, as legacy attainments).<br /> <br /> But on the grand scale of things, a +1 yantra bonus for fueling with appropriate resonance isn't that powerful for mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T04:16:45-07:00","id":1539139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1520861-fallen-magic?p=1520917#post1520917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth asking what your actual goal is in seeking a compilation of &quot;mortal magic,&quot; because as a category that's not really useful unless you're doing an extremely loose crossover game where the fact that theoretically any effect can be produced from a number of different ludonarrative frameworks is winning out over the general preferability that such systems as are used in a game for a single purpose be elegantly made. Sorcery is made to serve the purposes of sorcerers in a Mummy game, while Ceremonies are made to serve the needs of krewes in a Geist game, just as skinchangers and Shadow Occultists use different systems, and as ever, a Merit-based microtemplate is typically the means of enabling access to a variety of powers with the least amount of homebrew effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about other people, but my goal would be that I want my <i>character</i> to be the kind of cynical merit-grubber that Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle warned against. Going for a John Constantine thing, doing a lot with a little, making questionable bargains all over the place to build a deep library of tricks. And yes, I expect this to come back to bite my character. That's part of the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}